WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.440
Millions of people around the world have type 1 diabetes. Insulin and other supplies are part of daily life. Reliable access matters, every day.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:20.686
Sometimes, a supply runs low. People turn to family, friends, or small T1D groups. But help can be hard to find beyond those circles.

00:00:21.236 --> 00:00:32.012
After a real personal experience, VoiceOfT1D created this web exchange to help a wider community find one another. A mobile app is a future goal.

00:00:32.562 --> 00:00:37.290
Meet Maya. She needs a CGM and hopes to find one nearby.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.208
Meanwhile, Jordan has an unopened CGM he can offer.

00:00:42.758 --> 00:00:48.326
Maya shares what she needs and adds a city or ZIP. No street address needed.

00:00:48.876 --> 00:00:52.788
She spots a possible match and asks Jordan to connect.

00:00:53.338 --> 00:00:59.266
Jordan gets to decide. Maya's contact details stay private until he approves.

00:00:59.816 --> 00:01:05.504
He approves. Now they can share contact details and talk through what works for them.

00:01:06.054 --> 00:01:17.982
And that's the heart of this exchange. Insulin, test strips, CGM or pump supplies, and more. When something runs low, people can find each other and offer a hand.
